# hisn leak suite — manifest of expected test ids.
#
# run.sh FAILS at the end if any listed id produced no line (PASS/FAIL/SKIP/WEAK).
# This catches a test that was silently dropped from the suite.
#
# Format: one id per line, comments and blank lines ignored.
#
# HOST tests: ids marked HOST in the test comments (L53–L55, L56, L61, L72–L75)
# run on a host where 'hisn check' passes (user namespaces usable) and skip
# in CI (where hisn check fails and the suite exits at preflight). The
# needs_host() helper gates them on capability, not on an env var or hostname.
#
# L80 (host-service process-group stop, 0.4.3): the host service binds its
# socket in the case's own $WORK cwd and spawns a child via subprocess; the
# release gate cannot run it inside a live hisn session (it needs a real
# host), so it runs only on the host gate.
#
# L81 (dead host service, 0.4.3): the service exits 7 at once; the case
# asserts the literal "exited with status 7 before readiness completed"
# text, which the forward step can never produce (the socket path in the
# case never exists, so a forward failure would name the socket, not the
# status), and bounds the elapsed time well below the 30 s timeout.
